module main

-- §14.4 soundness (NEGATIVE): with `instance IsSet (List a)` deliberately
-- removed (it is FALSE — `List a` is a set only when `a` is), a generic
-- equality `(=) xs ys` over an ABSTRACT element type `a` is NOT an h-prop, so
-- `unsafeAssertProof` cannot construct it: the IsProp-under-Pi closure solver
-- reaches `IsProp ((=) xs ys)` over carrier `List a`, finds no
-- `IsSet (List a)` evidence, refuses to fabricate set-ness, and the assertion
-- is REJECTED (E_UNSOLVED_IMPLICIT).
--
-- Were `IsSet (List a)` reinstated, `bogus` below would type-check and a
-- `subst` over a discriminator type family would transport `Unit` into `Void`,
-- inhabiting `Void` — the same soundness catastrophe pinned closed for `Bool`
-- in `isprop-eq-requires-isset-bool-subst-rejected.kp`. List's monoid laws are
-- instead PROVEN by honest structural induction (see `listAppendAssoc`).

bogus : forall (a : Type) (xs : List a) (ys : List a). (=) xs ys
let bogus = unsafeAssertProof "spec-forbidden: List a is not a set at abstract a"

--! mode check
--! allow_unsafe_assert_proof
--! assertDiagnostic error E_UNSOLVED_IMPLICIT
